Checkpoint 22 package-integrity repair
Date: 2026-09-15

Reproduction:
- A fresh ZIP extraction was clean at commit 8c2efd97925236214b3dd1b67efa12b43a55b279.
- Direct `python3 scripts/validate_v09_docs.py --json` failed DOC-CMD-017 and DOC-CMD-018 with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'scripts'`.
- T0 had masked the defect because scripts/ci.sh exports PYTHONPATH="$PROJECT_ROOT/src:$PROJECT_ROOT".

Root cause:
- Direct script execution puts the repository `scripts/` directory on sys.path but not its parent repository root.
- `validate_v09_docs.py` imported `from scripts import environment_acceptance_runner` without adding ROOT itself.
- Clean packaging correctly removed ignored/generated residue; packaging must not restore generated files to hide the import defect.

Repair:
- `validate_v09_docs.py` now adds both repository ROOT and SRC to sys.path explicitly.
- `test_v09_documentation_hardening.py` removes PYTHONPATH before launching the validator so the clean-package execution contract is regression-protected.

Narrow verification:
- `env -u PYTHONPATH python3 scripts/validate_v09_docs.py --json` -> PASS, 175 checks.
- `python3 -m unittest -v tests.unit.test_v09_documentation_hardening` -> PASS, 4/4.

Evidence boundary:
- Host/package-executability evidence only. No Raspberry Pi, SHT31, relay, PENGLIN, fan, wake/audio, reboot or no-login physical acceptance is claimed.

Second clean-execution finding during exact-commit refresh:
- `python3 scripts/environment_simulation_runner.py ...` failed with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'gonken_agent'` when no PYTHONPATH was supplied.
- Root cause was the same class of hidden CI/developer-environment dependency at the evidence-runner entry point.
- The runner now establishes ROOT/SRC itself before importing `gonken_agent`.
- The release-candidate integration test now removes PYTHONPATH before invoking both the simulation runner and readiness gate.
- Final package verification must rerun the evidence runner/readiness gate from a fresh extraction before delivery.

Repair-verification execution note:
- The first combined repair-verification command exceeded its 180-second bound while the release-candidate integration test was active. It is TIMEOUT evidence, not PASS.
- The active integration module was isolated rather than repeating the aggregate unchanged: 1/1 PASS in 19.052 s.
- The independent documentation/readiness unit follow-up passed 9/9.
- T0 passed after those isolated checks.
